## Build / install / runtime verify

The canonical recipe is in `<docs-hub>/00_shared-rules/verify-build.md`. Quick reference:

```bash
# Build (real device — Xcode 15+)
xcodebuild -project {{project}}.xcodeproj \
           -scheme {{scheme}} \
           -destination 'platform=iOS,id={{udid}}' \
           build
# verify: https://developer.apple.com/documentation/xcode/build-system

# Install to real device
ios-deploy --id {{udid}} --bundle build/Build/Products/Debug-iphoneos/{{app}}.app --justlaunch
# verify: https://github.com/ios-control/ios-deploy
# alternative (Xcode 15+): xcrun devicectl device install app --device {{udid}} {{app_path}}

# Launch (xcrun devicectl 15+)
xcrun devicectl process launch --device {{udid}} {{bundle_id}}

# Runtime log
idevicesyslog -u {{udid}} | tee .ai-workspace/diag/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)-${TASK}-log.txt
# verify: https://libimobiledevice.org
# alt: log stream --device {{udid}} --predicate 'subsystem == "{{bundle_id}}"'

# Screenshot
xcrun simctl io booted screenshot .ai-workspace/screenshots/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)-${TASK}-after.png
# real device: xcrun devicectl device snapshot --device {{udid}}

# Lint
swiftlint
# verify: https://github.com/realm/SwiftLint
```

> ⚠️ **macOS only**: building iOS apps requires Xcode, which is macOS-exclusive. Linux / Windows users cannot run this frontend's build locally — use CI (GitHub Actions macOS runners, etc.).

## Git identity

This frontend's Dev commits as `{{git_alias}}`. Run `git as-{{alias}} commit ...`. Plain `git commit` is blocked by the `check_commit_alias.sh` pre-commit hook.

## Branch convention

- Integration branch: `{{integration_branch}}` (typically `develop`)
- Per-task branches: `dev/{{git_alias}}/{slug}`
- Fast-forward merge; delete branch after merge

## Commit message style

- Imperative, ≤50 chars
- No AI traces — pre-commit hook `check_ai_traces.sh` blocks AI-trace keywords
- Reads like an engineer's notes-to-self

Examples for iOS:

```
fix: bind player surface unconditionally
refactor: extract WithPerceptionTracking helper
feat: reduce home tabs to 2
perf: defer LazyVStack initial render via task
```

## SwiftUI / TCA gotchas

When using TCA (The Composable Architecture):

- `@Perception.Bindable` + `WithPerceptionTracking` are paired — iOS 16 fallback requires both
- `Reducer` cases should match action names from product spec; verify literally before drafting
- `Effect` returning long-running work needs explicit cancellation in `onDisappear`
- Avoid `try?` on critical paths — silent failures are §0.5 reason-text anti-pattern

